Scope: **16 issues = 2 STALE, 1 DUPLICATE, 3 FIXED-NEEDS-VERIFICATION, 0 LIVE-DEFECT, 2 ENHANCEMENT, 8 UNCLASSIFIABLE.** Chips: #457, #455, #454, #429, #447, #441, #438, #427, #431, #423, #428, #424. Additions: #432, #440, #475, #482. Budget the identified evidence/comment work at **12–16 engineer hours, plus unbounded U investigation and the E ruling/gate work**. The practical first gain is narrow dispositions for #423/#455 and duplication #475; this is not yet a whole-layer HIGH move.

The following commands are **for a later executor**, not commands run in this planning pass. Use Bash 4+ for the existing associative-array key injector. Work on a recorded, clean main revision and keep all logs/images tied to it. The checked-in Parallels launcher invokes run.sh, whose live #868 pattern sweeps can stop/delete another breenix-named VM. Use an explicitly exclusive Parallels host with no other breenix-named VM, or repair #868 separately before this runtime brief. Do not run these alongside another Parallels gate. The setup below derives the selected VM only from this run's result file; it does not prescribe a broad cleanup.

