### Evidence-only closing-comment templates

Use these only after the stated evidence actually exists. Replace every bracketed field with a recorded value/path; never paste an unevaluated PASS. The template does not declare a tracker state. For the eight U issues, use an investigation note in the later workflow until the missing discriminator is available; no issue-wide closing evidence exists in this plan. For E issues, record the operator's exact scope ruling first. No comment or issue action was sent in this pass.

For a narrow stale condition or fully verified landing:

```text
#423
At main [full SHA], [path:line] contains [current condition].
Command: [exact command]
Recorded result: [literal exit status and relevant output]
Evidence: [this run's serial/capture/source audit path]
Scope checked: [the precise claim from the issue body].
Remaining separate claims, if any: [plain issue numbers and their evidence scope].
A gh issue close command will follow separately.
```

For the duplicate:

```text
#475 and #482 both request MSI/SPI delivery, removal of timer-driven HID polling, and BWM wake-based input consumption.
Command: layer_issue 475 482
Recorded result: the two snapshot bodies contain the quoted overlapping claims; #482 also carries MSI programming-order detail.
Canonical evidence thread: #482.
Evidence: [snapshot path/date plus the exact compared quotations; any independently verified runtime capture]
This scope comparison makes no claim about guest input health.
A gh issue close command will follow separately.
```

The two commands are literal future actions, not automatic-keyword links. Before any separate tracker action, confirm the live issue has no newer unresolved scope and attach the actual evidence required above. After all legitimate dispositions, perform a fresh open-issue ownership sweep, repair the atlas's stale prose, and apply the operator's evidence/eligibility rule. The full-text absence of a standing GUI gate remains a blocker even if all sixteen issue IDs eventually receive dispositions.

### Separate lean PRs

There is **no confirmed LIVE-DEFECT in the selected cell's sixteen-issue roster**, so this pass prescribes **no kernel fix PR** for it. The eight U entries must identify a producing defect before a lean PR can be titled and scoped honestly. If such a producer is found, one defect per PR, with the exact failing/negative oracle established first; any Tier-1/Tier-2 change carries the required permission/justification and no hot-path logging. The known external GPU-DMA #493 and launcher #868 are not erased by this selection: #493 is owned by graphics/driver code in row 17, and #868 qualifies the runtime host setup above. Reclassify ownership if the evidence shows a GUI issue shares either producer.

This document is the sole file produced by the sweep. No repository source, input snapshot, atlas, prior plan, GitHub issue, branch or remote was changed by this pass; no kernel was built or booted, and no QEMU process was started.
